# Dependencies. There are none, and there should never be any: a dependency-free
# parser is the property most of this package's appeal rests on, so `node_modules`
# showing up here should be treated as a bug rather than a normal install step.

node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Pack artefacts. `npm pack` writes `<name>-<version>.tgz` into the repository
# root — verified, not assumed — and it is a build product with a version in its
# name, so it goes stale the moment the version moves and would otherwise sit in
# `git status` forever. It is also ~150 kB of duplicated tree.
#
# Worth ignoring because the publish path is the weakest part of this project's
# story right now, so `npm pack` is likely to get run: `npm publish --dry-run`
# prints `+ MachO-Tools@0.1.0` and exits 0 on a name npm will refuse, because a
# dry run does not ask the registry whether a name is acceptable.
*.tgz

# Scratch from the suites. Both write only under `os.tmpdir()`, but a mutation
# check that crashed mid-run could leave a `mutcheck-*` directory behind if the
# temp root were redirected.
mutcheck-*
.tw-*

# AppleDouble and resource-fork sidecars.
#
# Not cargo-culted from a macOS `.gitignore` template. This repository's
# correctness argument rests on `test/fixtures/*.macho` being byte-exact, and
# `fixtures.mjs --check` compares every byte — so a `._populated.macho` sitting
# next to `populated.macho` is a file that is not part of the corpus but reads as
# if it were. They appear when the tree is copied onto a non-native filesystem
# (a Linux container, a Docker volume, a SMB share), which is also exactly how a
# reviewer clones this to check the claims, so this is a likelier path here than
# in an ordinary repository.
._*
.AppleDouble/
.LSOverride/

# Editor and OS.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
*.orig
*.rej
.idea/
.vscode/

# Build output from `scripts/build-sea.mjs`. Each file is a ~100 MB Node runtime
# with the tool embedded, so `dist/` is large and is regenerated by CI; it is not
# a source artefact and must never be committed. `scripts/` is source and is not
# ignored — only its output is.
dist/

# SEA scratch: the blob and config the build writes before injecting them into
# a copy of the node binary. Ignored independently of `dist/` so a build pointed
# elsewhere (the `--output-dir` flag exists for exactly this) cannot leave these
# in the tree.
sea-prep-*.blob
sea-config-*.json

# Internal strategy documents.
strategy/

# Scratch directories the CI-surface suites create.
#
# `test/action.mjs` builds a shell step's environment and `test/pages.mjs`
# assembles the Pages site, both in a temporary directory beside the repository
# root rather than in the OS temp directory — beside, so the assembled site's
# relative paths resolve the same way they will after a real deployment, which is
# the whole thing being tested. Each suite removes its own directory on the way
# out; these entries cover the case where it did not, which is a test that threw
# rather than a test that failed, and an untracked directory is exactly the
# signal that tells you which of the two happened.
_site_test/
.tmp-action-scratch/
.tmp-action-test/
macho-audit.sarif
